# Friends Included Finance

Working finance system for the fictional Friends Included Ltd wedding-guest business.

## Live workflow

1. A salesperson or Kevin submits a sale/expense through the website or Telegram.
2. Supabase stores the source record and the site reloads it from there.
3. The same reference is upserted into the appropriate Google Sheets tab, so a manager correction never creates a duplicate row.
4. Svetlana can correct a proposed split/allocation and approve it.
5. Telegram submissions receive a saved/failed result, and the linked private chat receives the manager decision.

## Demonstration roles

- Richard, Anastasia and Jean-Claude submit sales with a commission split totalling 100%.
- Kevin submits expenses with a category and proposed allocation.
- Svetlana is the only role allowed to approve or correct a record and link Telegram identities.

## Telegram

Open [@LindaFriendsIncludedBot](https://t.me/LindaFriendsIncludedBot), then send `/id`. In the website, select **Svetlana**, open **Link Telegram employee**, and paste the returned user ID and chat ID against the appropriate fictional employee. The page keeps a visible saved-link receipt.

Commands:

```text
/sale S01 | Customer | A or B | description | amount | Richard % | Anastasia % | Jean-Claude %
/expense E01 | description | Materials, Travel or Other | amount | A, B or overhead
```

Use each reference once: for example `S01` or `E01`. The bot and server refuse a duplicate reference safely. If a Google Sheets write fails after Supabase saves the source record, Svetlana can use **Retry Google Sheets sync**. The manager page also offers a readable Sheet rebuild from the Supabase source of truth.

## Configuration

Keep all credentials in Vercel environment variables only:

- `SUPABASE_URL`
- `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY`
- `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`
- `GOOGLE_SHEETS_SPREADSHEET_ID`
- `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL`
- `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY`

Set the Telegram webhook once after deployment by opening `/api/setup-telegram` on the deployed Vercel URL. Never put tokens or service-account keys in GitHub, the site, or the Sheet.
